ime(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":0.54,"IC50_Dark_value":0.54,"Method":"CCK-8","DOI":"10.3390/ph18081185","Year":2025,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-052513","value":"6.36","numeric":6.36}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"DNP","value":1.46,"value_relation":"=","std":0.4,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"10 mM PBS","pH":7.4,"temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1002/anie.202011273","year":2020,"record_id":"MLDB-001568","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"Partition coefficient of the complexes was measured by the shake-flask method.[4] Briefly,n-octanol saturated water was prepared by mixing an equal volume of octanol and water and shaking on a mechanical shaker for 24 h at room temperature. Solutions of the complexes were prepared in phosphate buffer (PBS, 10 mM, pH 7.4, presaturated with n-octanol, Vwater). About half of the solutions was mixed with a volume of water-saturated octanol (Voctanol) and the mixture was shaken for 24 h at room temperature, followed by centrifugation at 2500 rpm for 1514min to separate different phases. Pt content was quantified in initial and final aqueous phases by ICP-MS. The log PO/W was measured using the following equation log PO/W = log ([C]initial - [C]final)/[C]final."}]}